w: 1.~From Heaven a- bove to earth I come, To bear good news to ev- ery home; 
w: 2.~To you, this night, is born a Child Of Ma- ry, cho- sen mo- ther mild; 
w: 3.~'Tis Christ our God, Who far on high Had heard your sad and bit- ter cry; 
w: 4.~He brings those bless- ings long a- go Pre- pared by God for all be- low; 
w: 5.~These are the to- kens ye shall mark, The swadd- ling clothes and man- ger dark; 
w: 6.~Now let us all, with glad- some cheer, Fol- low the shep- herds, and draw near
w: 7.~Give heed, my heart, lift up thine eyes! What is it in yon man- ger lies?
w: 8.~Wel- come to earth, Thou no- ble Guest, Through Whom e'en wi- cked men are blest!
w: 9.~Ah, Lord, Who hast cre- a- ted all, How hast Thou made Thee weak and small,
w: 10.~Were earth a thou- sand times as fair, Be- set with gold and jew- els rare,
w: 11.~For vel- vets soft and sil- ken stuff Thou hast but hay and straw so rough,
w: 12.~Thus hath it pleased Thee to make plain The truth to us, poor fools and vain,
w: 13.~Ah, dear- est Je- sus, ho- ly Child, Make Thee a bed, soft, un- de- filed,
w: 14.~My heart for ver- y joy doth leap, My lips no more can si- lence keep,
w: 15.~Glo- ry to God in high- est Heaven, Who un- to man His Son hath given,
