w: This ten- der Child of low- ly birth, Shall be the joy of all * your earth. 
w: Him- self will your Sal- va- tion be, Him- self from sin will make * you free. 
w: That in His heaven- ly king- dom blest You may with us for- ev- * er rest. 
w: There shall ye find the young Child laid, By Whom the heav'ns and earth * were made. 
w: To see this won- drous Gift of God, Who hath His own dear Son _ be- stowed.
w: Who is this Child, so young and fair? The bless- èd Christ Child li- _ eth there!
w: Thou com'st to share our mis- er- y, What can we ren- der, Lord, _ to Thee!
w: To lie up- on the coarse dry grass, The food of hum- ble ox _ and ass.
w: She yet were far too poor to be A nar- row cra- dle, Lord, _ for Thee.
w: Where- on Thou King, so rich and great, As 'twere Thy heaven, art throned _ in state.
w: That this world's hon- or, wealth and might Are naught and worth- less in _ Thy sight.
w: Here in my poor heart's in- most shrine, That I may ev- er- more _ be Thine.
w: I too must sing, with joy- ful tongue, That sweet- est an- cient cra- _ dle song.
w: While an- gels sing, with pi- ous mirth, A glad New Year to all _ the earth.
